SETaP Week 3: Data Collection

This tutorial is designed to help teams collect data to support specifying the requirements for the project. 

Design an interview to help you gather information about your project idea. This information should help you build a better understanding of the problem, identify the core concepts and their possible representations, the relationships between these concepts and the functionality associated with them. 

Structure your interview to include (but not be limited to) questions about:
The process currently in use to address the problem you are exploring
Limitations of the process
Need for a different solution
The definition of the key concept and the relationships between these concepts
Stakeholders involved
Goals of each stakeholder
Core functionality required
